The four test layers of (`tab:nrz:cas-series-design-tests`) include an independent small-integer/rational arithmetic oracle, independent inverse coefficients and both inverse compositions. Inverse fixtures bind every free coefficient explicitly before constructing their input objects, without presenting that member as free-family coverage. Mutations extend the equation range, omit the initial equation, fix or omit the terminal free column, embed an unknown into Q or K, let a parameter escape, change a parameter identity or specialization value, erase localization before cancellation, delete a zero-pivot branch or contradiction, and falsify either inverse composition. Each must preserve the distinctions above and those of (`tab:nrz:cas-series-design-mutations`). Complete production, supplied-candidate checking, map checking, export and fresh import have successful Work ceiling N and refusal at N−1 with identical prior spend, reuse state and other ceilings, including atomic rollback and retained evidence checks (`rule:nrz:cas-series-design-budget`). No measured cost or limit change is specified here.

